BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chi Kung
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260428T173000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260428T183000
UID:88dd4750dbda96ad08cd3cfa@lbc-ics
DESCRIPTION:Chi Kung is an ancient Chinese system of exercises that help u
 s contact and harness energy in the body\, and can be a great way to prepa
 re for meditation. Join us for a beginner-friendly session led by Serene. 
 No experience necessary.
URL:https://www.londonbuddhistcentre.com/whats-on/chi-kung-28-apr
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:PoetryEAST with Jane Hirshfield
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260428T183000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260428T213000
UID:e98ba6c7e31a2a551abf81ab@lbc-ics
DESCRIPTION:A rare chance to meet the American poet\, Jane Hirshfield on h
 er first visit to London since 2007. Jane will be reading from The Asking:
  New & Selected Poems (2024). She’ll be in conversation with Maitreyaban
 dhu in a special celebration of her work at the Mandala Café. Come for a 
 wonderful vegan meal on sale from 6.30pm\, with the readings and conversat
 ion starting around 7.15pm.
URL:https://www.londonbuddhistcentre.com/whats-on/poetryeast-with-jane-hir
 shfield
END:VEVENT
